From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: ps3fb: remember that the RSX driver gave the GPU up not idle

ps3fb keeps the lv1 GPU context across loads of the RSX driver (ps3rsx).
When ps3rsx unloads with a job still running or the GPU stalled, it keeps
the GPU from ps3fb ("keeping it from ps3fb until reboot"): PGRAPH may run
on. A module loaded afterwards would run FIFO_SETUP on that context under
the old job, a hardware state nobody has tested (round 3 review, R4).

The state has to outlive the module, so it lives in ps3fb next to
gpu_recovered:

- ps3fb_gpu_release_busy(): ps3rsx calls it when it gives the GPU up not
  idle. Refused (-EPERM) unless someone
  holds the GPU, and after ps3fb has shut down. Sticky, once; only a reboot clears it. No lv1 call.
- ps3fb_gpu_released_busy(): tells a later ps3rsx, which refuses to load.
- ps3fb_gpu_takeover() answers -EBUSY from then on, true or false, so a
  driver that doesn't ask is stopped too, and ps3fb's FIFO is never
  restored under the old job (as after a recovery).
- ps3fb's shutdown leaves the contexts to lv1 when the flag is set, as it
  does after a recovery, instead of freeing a context PGRAPH may still use.

Nothing on a hot path changes: the flag is read and written under
gpu_own_lock at load, unload and takeover only. ps3rsx looks the two
calls up at run time (symbol_get), so a ps3rsx built for an older kernel
without them still loads.

Forwarded: no
---
diff --git a/arch/powerpc/include/asm/ps3gpu.h b/arch/powerpc/include/asm/ps3gpu.h
--- a/arch/powerpc/include/asm/ps3gpu.h
+++ b/arch/powerpc/include/asm/ps3gpu.h
@@ -116,4 +116,8 @@ int ps3fb_gpu_ctx_leak(const struct ps3fb_gpu_hook *hook);
 int ps3fb_gpu_ctx_realloc(const struct ps3fb_gpu_hook *hook, u64 handle, struct ps3fb_gpu_ctx *ctx);
 bool ps3fb_gpu_recovered(void);
 
+/* The RSX driver gave the GPU up not idle: no new owner until reboot (see ps3fb.c) */
+int ps3fb_gpu_release_busy(void);
+bool ps3fb_gpu_released_busy(void);
+
 #endif /* _ASM_POWERPC_PS3GPU_H */
diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/ps3fb.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/ps3fb.c
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/ps3fb.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/ps3fb.c
@@ -227,6 +227,7 @@ static u64 gpu_ctx_iomap[256];		/* lpar mapped at each 1 MiB IO page of gpu_ctx,
  * after a recovery shut the console down (2026-11-01), and lv1 cleans up the LPAR at reboot.
  */
 static bool gpu_recovered;	/* under gpu_own_lock: a recovery began (once per boot) */
+static bool gpu_released_busy;	/* under gpu_own_lock: ps3rsx gave the GPU up not idle; sticky until reboot */
 static bool gpu_ctx_leaked;	/* under both locks: the driver context was leaked */
 static u64 gpu_ctx_leaked_handle;	/* under gpu_own_lock: never freed, never reallocated */
 static unsigned int gpu_ctx_reallocs;	/* under gpu_own_lock: at most one per boot */
@@ -2599,6 +2600,10 @@ int ps3fb_gpu_takeover(bool own)
 		ret = -EBUSY;		/* after a recovery ps3fb's channel 0 is never run again */
 		goto out;
 	}
+	if (gpu_released_busy) {
+		ret = -EBUSY;		/* the last owner left a job or a stall behind: no new FIFO setup, no handback */
+		goto out;
+	}
 	if (own == gpu_owned)
 		goto out;
 	if (own && gpu_direct && ps3gpu_direct_owner_gone())
@@ -2792,6 +2797,42 @@ bool ps3fb_gpu_recovered(void)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ps3fb_gpu_recovered);
 
+/*
+ * ps3rsx gave the GPU up without having it idle (its drain timed out, or the GPU was wedged) and
+ * keeps it from ps3fb: the old job may still run in PGRAPH. A module loaded later must not run
+ * FIFO_SETUP on this context under it, and the flag has to outlive the module, so it lives here,
+ * next to gpu_recovered. Pure software state, no lv1 call. Sticky: only a reboot clears it. The
+ * call is refused (-EPERM) unless someone holds the GPU (gpu_owned); there is no check of who
+ * calls, as the hook is already cleared by then. Any GPL module could set the flag, and all it
+ * does is make ps3fb_gpu_takeover() refuse, so it is no way to get at the GPU.
+ */
+int ps3fb_gpu_release_busy(void)
+{
+	int ret = 0;
+
+	mutex_lock(&gpu_own_lock);
+	if (shadow.dead || !gpu_owned) {
+		ret = -EPERM;
+	} else if (!gpu_released_busy) {
+		gpu_released_busy = true;
+		pr_warn("%s: the GPU was released not idle: no new owner until reboot\n", __func__);
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&gpu_own_lock);
+	return ret;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ps3fb_gpu_release_busy);
+
+bool ps3fb_gpu_released_busy(void)
+{
+	bool r;
+
+	mutex_lock(&gpu_own_lock);
+	r = gpu_released_busy;
+	mutex_unlock(&gpu_own_lock);
+	return r;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ps3fb_gpu_released_busy);
+
 static void ps3fb_gpu_vma_open(struct vm_area_struct *vma) {}
 static void ps3fb_gpu_vma_close(struct vm_area_struct *vma) {}
 
@@ -3152,7 +3193,7 @@ static void ps3fb_shutdown(struct ps3_system_bus_device *dev)
 	mutex_unlock(&shadow_lock);
 	mutex_lock(&gpu_own_lock);
 	shadow.dead = true;
-	recovered = gpu_recovered;
+	recovered = gpu_recovered || gpu_released_busy;
 	put_pid(gpu_direct_owner);	/* a direct session just stops: the context goes */
 	gpu_direct_owner = NULL;
 	mutex_unlock(&gpu_own_lock);
